knowledge:
- key_parameters:
  - ribo.object / x = The initialized Ribo class object representing the .ribo file. ;;
  - range.lower = The lower bound of the ribosome protected footprint (RPF) read lengths to analyze (e.g., 28). ;;
  - range.upper = The upper bound of the ribosome protected footprint (RPF) read lengths to analyze (e.g., 32). ;;
  - length = Logical; if TRUE, counts are summed across the specified read length interval. If FALSE, counts at each individual read length are reported separately. ;;
  - transcript = Logical; if TRUE, counts are summed across all transcripts. If FALSE, counts at each individual transcript are reported separately. ;;
  - alias = Logical; if TRUE, uses shortened transcript names (aliases) instead of long reference names. ;;
  - compact = Logical; if TRUE (default), returns an S4 Vectors DataFrame with Rle and factor columns to minimize memory footprint. If FALSE, returns a standard data.frame. ;;
  - tidy = Logical; if TRUE (default), returns data in a tidy format. If FALSE, returns non-tidy format. ;;
  - region = Character vector specifying transcript regions (e.g., "UTR5", "UTR5J", "CDS", "UTR3J", "UTR3"). ;;
  - site = Character specifying "start" or "stop" site for metagene analysis. ;;
  - rename = A function or string vector used to rename transcripts when initializing the Ribo object.
- alternatives: None mentioned. The documentation notes that .ribo files are generated using the RiboFlow pipeline and can be inspected using the RiboPy ecosystem.
- when_to_use: Use this package when you have ribosome profiling data processed into the .ribo format and want to perform quality control (read length distribution, metagene coverage around start/stop codons), region-specific quantification (5'UTR, CDS, 3'UTR and their junctions), and translational efficiency analysis when paired with RNA-Seq data.
- pitfalls:
  - Do not manually modify the values of the returned Ribo object, as downstream functions rely on its internal list structure. ;;
  - Setting transcript = FALSE and length = FALSE simultaneously in get_metagene can result in slow run times and require a substantial amount of memory. ;;
  - Setting compact = FALSE returns a standard data.frame instead of an S4 DataFrame, which can double the memory footprint of the returned object. ;;
  - Some transcripts might have very short regions compared to left/right spans, causing modified region coordinates to be marked as NA and lengths as 0. ;;
  - When using read_multiple_files, the compact parameter must be set to FALSE, and properties across Ribo objects must be consistent (e.g., same aliases, RNA-Seq, coverage availability).
